From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:06:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] soc: mediatek: mt6797-a72: bring the cluster back on a
 scaled VPROC2

The cluster's preparation after both A72s were down required BUCKB at
1.0 V, as the preloader leaves it. With A72 voltage scaling, VPROC2 is
wherever the last operating point left it, so the A72s could not come
back.

Accept VPROC2 from its 880 mV floor to 1.2 V when preparing the cluster
again. The firmware's CPU_ON starts it at 750 MHz, which the floor
covers, and the clock driver puts the last rate back. The first bring-up
at module load still requires 1.0 V.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-a72.c | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-a72.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-a72.c
index ed3aa57ad..3ecf6fa4d 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-a72.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-a72.c
@@ -62,6 +62,9 @@
 #define DA9214_VBUCKB_A			0xd9
 #define DA9214_VBUCKB_B			0xda
 #define  DA9214_VBUCKB_1000MV		0x46
+/* 300 mV + 10 mV a step: VPROC2's floor and top under voltage scaling. */
+#define  DA9214_VBUCKB_880MV		0x3a
+#define  DA9214_VBUCKB_1200MV		0x5a
 
 #define SMC_REG_READ			0xc200035fUL
 #define SMC_SRAM_LDO_SET		0xc20003bfUL
@@ -126,6 +129,20 @@ static int buck_expect(struct mt6797_a72 *a72, u8 reg, u8 expected)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int buck_expect_range(struct mt6797_a72 *a72, u8 reg, u8 min, u8 max)
+{
+	int val = i2c_smbus_read_byte_data(a72->buck, reg);
+
+	if (val < 0)
+		return val;
+	if (val < min || val > max) {
+		dev_err(a72->dev, "DA9214 0x%02x is 0x%02x, expected 0x%02x-0x%02x\n",
+			reg, val, min, max);
+		return -ERANGE;
+	}
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int pwrap_reset_expect(struct mt6797_a72 *a72, int expected)
 {
 	int status = reset_control_status(a72->pwrap_reset);
@@ -200,7 +217,17 @@ static int mt6797_a72_check_off(struct mt6797_a72 *a72, bool rail_on)
 			DA9214_BUCKB_CONT, buck);
 		return -ERANGE;
 	}
-	ret = buck_expect(a72, DA9214_VBUCKB_A, DA9214_VBUCKB_1000MV);
+	/*
+	 * After the A72s have been down, a voltage consumer may have left
+	 * VPROC2 anywhere from its 880 mV floor to 1.2 V. The firmware's CPU_ON
+	 * starts the cluster at 750 MHz, which the floor covers.
+	 */
+	if (rail_on)
+		ret = buck_expect_range(a72, DA9214_VBUCKB_A,
+					DA9214_VBUCKB_880MV,
+					DA9214_VBUCKB_1200MV);
+	else
+		ret = buck_expect(a72, DA9214_VBUCKB_A, DA9214_VBUCKB_1000MV);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 	return buck_expect(a72, DA9214_VBUCKB_B, DA9214_VBUCKB_1000MV);
